msgid "Qiskit Paulice {#qiskit-paulice}"
msgstr "Qiskit Paulice {#qiskit-paulice}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`qiskit-paulice` is a package for embedding hardware-efficient Pauli checks into arbitrary Clifford circuits on arbitrary qubit connectivities using spacetime stabilizer codes. These checks can be used to detect logical errors during circuit execution. Postselecting only samples with no detected errors can improve the fidelity of states sampled with a quantum processor at the cost of some ancilla qubits and an increase in sampling overhead. This method is particularly suited to near-term hardware since it has a much milder overhead in qubits and gates compared to fault-tolerant quantum computing, while having a better sampling overhead than error mitigation methods such as ZNE or PEC [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"
msgstr "Ang `qiskit-paulice` ay isang package para sa pag-embed ng mga hardware-efficient na Pauli check sa arbitraryong Clifford circuit sa arbitraryong qubit connectivity gamit ang spacetime stabilizer codes. Magagamit ang mga check na ito para madetect ang mga logical error habang tumatakbo ang circuit. Ang pag-postselect ng mga sample na walang natukoy na error ay makapagpapabuti ng fidelity ng mga state na sinample gamit ang quantum processor kapalit ng ilang ancilla qubit at pagtaas ng sampling overhead. Angkop na angkop ang pamamaraang ito sa near-term hardware dahil mas banayad ang overhead nito sa mga qubit at gate kumpara sa fault-tolerant quantum computing, habang mas maganda ang sampling overhead nito kaysa sa mga error mitigation method tulad ng ZNE o PEC [\\[1\\]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Although spacetime Pauli checks may be used to implement standalone error detection routines, they are also relevant in the context of error mitigation and error correction. Error detection can complement error mitigation techniques such as probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) by capturing some of the noise affecting gates and measurements, reducing the impact of the noise channel being inverted and thus reducing the sampling overhead. They can also be viewed as an early step toward practical fault tolerance, since implementing stabilizer codes to protect data qubits from logical errors is a core concept of traditional error correction. Since this method provides single-shot access to the quantum state, it can be used in both sampling-based and expectation value-based workflows.\n"
msgstr "Kahit magagamit ang spacetime Pauli checks para magpatupad ng standalone na error detection routine, may kaugnayan din ang mga ito sa error mitigation at error correction. Maaaring umakma ang error detection sa mga error mitigation technique tulad ng probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) sa pamamagitan ng pagkuha ng bahagi ng noise na nakaaapekto sa mga gate at measurement, na nagpapababa sa epekto ng noise channel na iniinvert at kaya nagpapababa ng sampling overhead. Maaari rin silang ituring na maagang hakbang tungo sa praktikal na fault tolerance, dahil ang pagpapatupad ng stabilizer codes para protektahan ang mga data qubit mula sa logical error ay pangunahing konsepto ng tradisyonal na error correction. Dahil nagbibigay ang pamamaraang ito ng single-shot na access sa quantum state, magagamit ito sa parehong sampling-based at expectation value-based na workflow.\n"

